60,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: The options are on the table. A is flat, B is seasonal fixed, C is per-room metering. Let’s weigh them.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Mio,,- **Mio**: Option C sounds like a nightmare for my evenings. I’d rather not spend forty minutes logging readings every month.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"- **Jonathan**: Option C ignores the shared areas, which is where the real confusion starts. I find it incomplete.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: Option C’s upfront cost is prohibitive. I cannot justify that expense without seeing a clear, long-term reduction in my winter bills.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I worry Option C makes us feel like we are always checking on each other. I prefer something that keeps us together.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: Option B smooths the February spike. You pay a set amount, and the year-end settle handles the rest.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mio,,"- **Mio**: @Benjamin, does the year-end settle mean I’m doing the math again? I need to know the time cost.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: Option B respects the seasonal reality without the arbitrary lot system. It feels more honest than a flat split.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Victoria,,- **Victoria**: The year-end reconciliation is a heavy lift. I need to know if the fixed rate actually protects me from that February shock.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Minato,,- **Minato**: I like that Option B feels steady. It might stop the awkwardness before it starts.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"- **Benjamin**: @Mio, the year-end settle is a one-time task, not a monthly grind. It’s manageable.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mio,,- **Mio**: One big task is better than twelve small ones. I can handle that.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: Option B acknowledges the physical reality of the rooms without the high cost of meters. It feels the most balanced.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: If the fixed rate covers the February spike, I can accept the year-end reconciliation. It is a fair trade.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: I think Option B is the kindest. It feels steady, and I hope it helps us stop feeling awkward about the money.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,- **Benjamin**: I agree. Option B balances the seasonal reality with manageable effort. I vote for B.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mio,,- **Mio**: I vote for B. One big task at year-end is much better than monthly headaches.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,- **Jonathan**: I vote for B. It reflects the actual usage patterns without the high upfront cost of meters.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"- **Victoria**: I vote for B. The predictable rate protects me from the winter shock, and the year-end settle is acceptable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Minato,,"- **Minato**: I vote for B. It feels steady and kind, and I hope it helps us feel safe with each other again.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
